course: dictionary
lesson: 5268
title: Joy and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word joy can mean a feeling, or a thing that causes the feeling. The words around it show you which one. «The new puppy filled the whole house with joy.» Here joy is a big happy feeling, because the puppy has made everyone feel glad.
explain: Joy can also name a person or thing that makes you happy. «The new puppy is a joy to be with.» Here the puppy is the joy, because it is the thing that makes people happy. Ask yourself: is joy the feeling here, or the thing that causes it?
explain: In UK informal speech, joy can mean luck or success. «Any joy finding your keys?» is a question about luck, not about happiness. The question mark and the word any are your clues. Try swapping in luck or success: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Joy means a feeling of great happiness.
fact: A joy can also be a person or thing that makes you very happy.
fact: In UK informal speech, «any joy» can mean success or luck.
fact: «Jump for joy» means to jump because you are very happy, and «cry with joy» means to cry because you are very happy.
fact: «Bundle of joy» means a newborn baby, and «pride and joy» means the thing you care for most.
exercise: «The children jumped for joy when the snow began to fall.» What does joy mean here? | A tool for digging | A person in charge of the class | Cold, wet weather | *A feeling of great happiness
exercise: Sam says «a joy to be with» means someone who is very sad. What does a joy mean here? | *Someone who makes you very happy | Someone who is hard to find | Someone who makes you very sad | A room where you sleep
exercise: «Any joy finding your keys?» What does any joy mean here? | *Luck or success | A newborn baby | A feeling of being cold | A long, sad sigh
test: Which phrase means a newborn baby? | *Bundle of joy | Pride and joy | Jump for joy | Cry with joy
test: What does «pride and joy» mean? | A quiet room | *The thing you care for most | A bill you must pay | A bad storm
exam: In the sentence «Her joy was clear to see», what does joy mean? | *Great happiness | Sadness | A loud noise | Tiredness
